      "skos:prefLabel": "Event-driven architecture",
      "skos:definition": "An architecture style in which decoupled services communicate by publishing, routing and consuming events (records of state changes) through an event router or messaging service instead of calling each other directly; on AWS it is typically built with EventBridge, SNS, SQS, Lambda and Step Functions.",
