      "@id": "kt:microservices-architecture",
      "@type": "kto:Pattern",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Microservices architecture",
      "skos:definition": "An architectural style that splits an application into small, independently deployable services that own their data, communicate through well-defined APIs or events and are run by autonomous teams; AWS frames it as a reliability and agility choice whose distributed-system costs must be weighed against a modular monolith.",
      "kto:domain": "architecture-practice",
